    "cols2_2_3_1_3_124826_2117329145": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:22 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:22 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_copy": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:26 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Dr. Burke&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Nov 25 2019 17:50:31 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "sectionseparator": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:25:54 GMT+0000",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:25:54 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/sectionseparator"
        },
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:26 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>A sense of humor and humility are the qualities used to describe Dr. Vernon Burke by those who know him. His personable nature lends to his success in working with children, and in particular, those afflicted with craniofacial and cleft anomalies.</p>\n<p>Born in Idaho, and a Gulf War veteran, Dr. Burke is the Department Chair of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery and Pediatric/Hospital Dentistry at El Paso Children’s Hospital. He and his partners have three clinic locations in El Paso, and in 2018, Dr. Burke co-founded the Cleft and Craniofacial Clinic at Federacion Mexicana de Asociaciones Privadas (FEMAP) Hospital in Juarez, Mexico.</p>\n<p>He’s no stranger to complex craniofacial deformities, performing, on average, 450 surgeries per year with a focus on bony work for cleft and craniofacial surgery and orthognathic surgery. It is this expertise, and the proximity and connection to Juarez, that led to his fateful meeting with Olivia.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Dec 09 2019 14:29:03 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
