    "cols2_2_3_1_3_124826_132795843": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:22 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:22 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_copy": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:26 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Finding her guide, the path to a better outcome&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Nov 25 2019 17:52:17 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "sectionseparator": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:25:54 GMT+0000",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:25:54 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/sectionseparator"
        },
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 22 2019 20:05:26 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>When Karen, a former patient of Dr. Burke’s in El Paso, saw Olivia’s story featured on the local television in Juarez, she knew she had to connect Olivia with Dr. Burke. After locating Olivia’s mother, Karen was able to help get an appointment with Dr. Burke at his Juarez FEMAP clinic.</p>\n<p>Before the first appointment, Olivia was becoming ill multiple times per year and wasn’t eating well. On top of that, she was living with a one in ten risk of death each year that she had the tracheostomy tube.</p>\n<p>Dr. Burke’s immediate goal in the first six to eight months of treatment was to open her airways via a distraction procedure, and subsequently remove the distractors, with the end goal to remove the tracheostomy. The procedure was complex, and Vanessa was not supported by health insurance, so Dr. Burke formulated a plan to garner support needed for her procedure.</p>\n<p>In addition to the time donated by Dr. Burke and other surgeons and staff, Olivia’s surgery would need a pediatric mandibular distraction system, which Stryker donated. In addition, El Paso Children’s Hospital donated an operating room and 3D Systems donated medical models and Virtual Surgical Planning services.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Nov 25 2019 17:53:19 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
